-- title:
--   Hecke words annihilating the new lattice kill new parabolic homomorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ and $q'$ be natural numbers with $q'$ prime and $q' \nmid N$, and let $A$ be an Atkin–Lehner datum for the level $Nq'$ and the prime $q'$, that is, a natural number $R$ with $Nq' = q'R$ together with integers $a,b$ satisfying $q'a - Rb = 1$. Let $P$ be an element of the free associative $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra on the set $\mathbb{N}$, thought of as a word in Hecke symbols. Assume $P$ annihilates the new lattice $\mathtt{CuspForm.newLattice}\,A\,hq'$, i.e. the image of $P$ under the algebra map $\mathtt{CuspForm.heckeWordForms}$ (which sends a generator $n$ to the Hecke operator at $n$ when $n$ is prime and $n \nmid Nq'$, and to $0$ otherwise) kills every weight-$2$ cusp form $f$ on $\Gamma_0(Nq')$ such that for every $t$ in the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of endomorphisms generated by the Hecke generators away from the primes dividing $Nq'$, the form $t f$ lies in the lattice spanned by forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients and satisfies $\mathrm{tr}_A(tf) = 0$ and $\mathrm{tr}_A(W_A(tf)) = 0$, where $\mathrm{tr}_A$ is the level-lowering trace to level $R$ and $W_A$ the Atkin–Lehner involution attached to $A$. Let $\varphi : \Gamma_0(Nq') \to \mathbb{Z}$ be a homomorphism (from the group written additively) which is parabolic, i.e. $\varphi(\gamma) = 0$ for every $\gamma$ whose trace satisfies $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma)^2 = 4$, and assume both degeneracy transfers $\mathtt{HeckeEis.degeneracyTransfer₀}\ N\ q'\ \mathbb{Z}$ and $\mathtt{HeckeEis.degeneracyTransfer₁}\ N\ q'\ \mathbb{Z}$ vanish on $\varphi$. Then the image of $P$ under the algebra map $\mathtt{HeckeEis.heckeWordHom}$ (sending a generator $n$ to the Hecke operator on homomorphisms when $n$ is prime and $n \nmid Nq'$, and to $0$ otherwise) annihilates $\varphi$.
--
--   This is the cohomological half of the Eichler–Shimura dictionary in its annihilator form, restricted to the $q'$-new part: an element of the anemic Hecke algebra that kills the $q'$-new lattice of weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(Nq')$ also kills every integral parabolic homomorphism lying in the common kernel of the two degeneracy transfers to level $N$. It is used in the level-raising argument, in [`LevelRaising.qNewSupport_comap_of_isNormalizedEigenform_oddPrime`](thm.html#LevelRaising.qNewSupport_comap_of_isNormalizedEigenform_oddPrime).
